language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Give candies to children standing in a line: each child gets at least one, a child with a higher rating than a neighbour gets more candies than that neighbour, and the total number of candies is minimised.
given ratings_dim1 : int(1..)
given ratings : matrix indexed by [int(1..ratings_dim1)] of int
$ each child gets at least one candy; the upper bound is the number of children, since the optimal allocation never needs more (a longest run of rising ratings has at most that many children)
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..ratings_dim1)] of int(1..ratings_dim1)
find z : int(0..ratings_dim1 * ratings_dim1)

minimising z
such that
$ the total number of candies is the sum of the candies given to each child
z = (sum i : int(1..ratings_dim1) . x[i]),
$ a child with a higher rating than the next child gets more candies than the next child
forAll i : int(1..ratings_dim1 - 1) . (ratings[i] > ratings[i+1]) -> (x[i] > x[i+1]),
$ a child with a lower rating than the next child gets fewer candies than the next child
forAll i : int(1..ratings_dim1 - 1) . (ratings[i] < ratings[i+1]) -> (x[i] < x[i+1])
